# OAuth Configuration
# Copy this file to oauth.conf and fill in your OAuth credentials.
#
# Neither provider's redirect URI below is read by api/server.py -- the
# frontend computes it dynamically per request (getRedirectUri() in
# web/src/components/OAuthButtons.jsx: `${protocol}//${host}/oauth/callback`)
# and sends it explicitly with every OAuth call. What matters is that the
# *provider's* console has the exact same URL registered -- your real
# admin-panel origin in production (e.g.
# https://minecraft-admin.yourdomain.com/oauth/callback), and
# http://localhost:5173/oauth/callback for local dev against the Vite
# server (see web/vite.config.js's `server.port`).

# Google OAuth Configuration
# Get these from: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# (create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "Web application")
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://minecraft-admin.yourdomain.com/oauth/callback

# Apple OAuth Configuration
# Get this from: https://developer.apple.com/account/resources/identifiers/list
# -- create a Services ID (not an App ID), enable "Sign In with Apple" on
# it, and configure it with your admin-panel domain and the redirect URI
# above. That Services ID's identifier (a reverse-DNS-style string, e.g.
# com.yourdomain.minecraft-admin) is APPLE_CLIENT_ID below.
#
# APPLE_TEAM_ID, APPLE_KEY_ID and APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY are NOT read by
# api/server.py -- this app's Apple flow only ever verifies the ID token
# Apple hands back (against Apple's own published JWKS), it never does a
# server-to-server token exchange, so none of the signing-key machinery
# those three normally support is needed. Left here as placeholders in
# case that ever changes; don't spend time generating a Sign In with Apple
# key for this app as it stands today.
APPLE_CLIENT_ID=your-apple-services-id
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
APPLE_KEY_ID=
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
APPLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://minecraft-admin.yourdomain.com/oauth/callback
